The duplicate-detection engine in this tool is an **independent (clean-room) implementation**.
Its design approach references BookOrbit's duplicate module
(https://github.com/bookorbit/bookorbit, AGPL-3.0-only with §7 additional terms).

What was referenced — ideas and structure only (methods, not protectable expression):
  · two-tier evidence ranking (exact ISBN stronger than fuzzy title match)
  · match reasons expressed as data (enum), rendered by the UI per locale
  · comparison showing only fields that differ between copies
  · keeper selection by tuple comparison (no ambiguous "tie score")
  · dismissals that survive a rescan

What was NOT used:
  · no BookOrbit code, constant tables, or data of any kind
  · no copy of its weight table, stop-word list, or provider identifier maps
  · all field sets, weights, thresholds and media-family rules are redefined for MyBooks/Calibre
  · Chinese text handling (character bigrams, variant scoring, trailing-annotation stripping)
    is this repository's own design; BookOrbit has no equivalent

This tool therefore carries **no AGPL obligation**: it contains none of BookOrbit's code and is
not derived from it. The LICENSE here is this tool's own (BSD-2-Clause, matching the MyBooks host).